theory:
## Preconditions with requires

A precondition is a condition that must hold BEFORE the function executes.

### Basic Syntax

```xiom
fn deposit(balance: &mut Int, amount: Int)
  requires: amount > 0;
{ balance = balance + amount; }
```

### Multiple requires Clauses

```xiom
fn set_age(person: &mut Person, age: Int)
  requires: age >= 0;
  requires: age <= 150;
{ person.age = age; }
```

Each requires is independent — all are checked, all violations reported.

### Order Is Meaningful

```xiom
fn access(arr: &Vec[Int], index: Int) -> Int
  requires: arr != null;        // Check existence first
  requires: index >= 0;         // Then validate index
  requires: index < arr.len();  // Then check bounds
{ return arr[index]; }
```

### What requires CAN'T Access

`requires` can only reference: parameters, global constants, and pure functions. No side effects or I/O.

